#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/07-text-processing.md:142
msgid "Remove spaces: `strip`"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-processing.md:144
msgid "`strip()` removes spaces (and tabs and new lines) at **both ends**; `lstrip()` only at the start, `rstrip()` only at the end:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-processing.md:155
msgid "With an argument, `strip` removes **those characters** from the ends (any of them, in any order) - not a word:"
msgstr ""

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/07-text-processing.md:165
msgid "Spaces inside: `COMPBL`"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-processing.md:167
msgid "`strip` does not touch the spaces **inside**. `split()` without an argument splits on any run of spaces, and `\" \".join(...)` puts the words back with one space:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-processing.md:177
msgid "`\" \".join(s.split())` is the standard Python idiom for \"remove all extra spaces\". Section 4 explains `split` and `join`."
msgstr ""

